<!-- 01 — THE SITUATION -->
<section class="container measure section-block section-block--tight">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">01 — The situation</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">The business has moved on, the brand presence has not</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">A company is acquired or makes an acquisition itself. The founding generation hands over. A single product has become a portfolio, a domestic business an international one. New products, new markets, a different focus – and a brand presence that still shows the company of five years ago. Prospects notice this before they call. Some then do not call.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">At the same time, the existing brand presence is an asset: customers, dealers and employees recognise it. Replacing it lightly means losing exactly the trust that has been built up over years.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-2">A relaunch has to do two things at once: show what is new, and keep what is recognised.</p>
</section>

<!-- 02 — DEPTH OF INTERVENTION -->
<section class="container measure section-block">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">02 — Only what changes</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Recognition is an asset that is carried forward</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Not every relaunch is a fresh start. Often most of it stays and only part changes: a symbol is dropped, a hierarchy is reordered, an addition is made. Sometimes, on the other hand, a completely new logo is the right answer. Which depth of intervention holds up is shown by the analysis – not by the wish for something new.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">The art then lies in making the new visible without losing the familiar – and in not overlooking a single application that still shows the old version.</p>
</section>

<!-- 03 — WHAT IS CREATED -->
<section class="container measure section-block">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">03 — What is created</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">From the logo to the last application</h2>
  <ul class="check-list">
    {%- for item in [
      "An analysis of which parts of the existing brand presence carry recognition and which stand in the way of the new direction",
