<!-- 04 — THE WEBSITE -->
<section class="container measure section-block">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">04 — The website</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Several visitors, several questions – and an AI assistant</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">An outdated brand presence usually shows first on the website. Not because it looks dated, but because it describes a company that no longer exists in that form. In B2B, it is visited not by one person but by several, with different questions. The engineer looks for data and evidence. Purchasing looks for delivery capability and a contact. Management wants to know whether the company will still be there in ten years.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-2">A website that addresses all three in the same way addresses none of them properly.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">More and more research also no longer starts in a search engine but with a question to an AI assistant. It recommends providers without linking – and only those whose website it can clearly understand. That takes no tricks, just clarity: who the company is, what it offers, for whom and with what evidence – in a form machines can read as well as people. This includes technology that loads fast and can be maintained without an agency, including ongoing operation if required.</p>
</section>

<!-- 05 — THE ROLLOUT -->
<section class="container measure section-block">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">05 — The rollout</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Hundreds of applications, one deadline</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">A new brand presence is decided once and applied a thousand times: on signs and vehicles, on products, in presentations, forms, signatures, on the website and in every video. If it is not rolled out in an orderly way, the old lives on alongside the new for a long time. Customers then see two senders – and wonder which one applies. Exactly what the decision was meant to end.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-2">A brand presence that is consistent only in the manual is not consistent.</p>
</section>

